LATENT DISPATCH
Mon Sep 21 · 5 items · ~4 min

LODESTONE-R2 MINI: REASONING FOR THE MID-TIER BUDGET
A distilled R2 at $0.80 / $3.20 per million. It keeps about 85% of R2's hard-reasoning score and is four times faster. For the "one careful call per workflow" pattern, this is probably the new default. https://latentdispatch.ai/p/r2-mini

COMMIT PRICING IS EVERYWHERE THIS MONTH
Kestrel started it, and now Argent, Nimbus, and two of the labs offer a quarterly or annual prepay discount of 10–20%. Our advice has not changed: with prices dropping 10–20% a month at the mid-tier, a 15% discount for a 12-month lock is not a discount. Quarterly at most.

NIMBUS POST-MORTEM
Clear and honest: a config change to the load balancer was rolled out globally instead of per-region. They are adding staged rollouts. Good write-up. https://latentdispatch.ai/p/nimbus-postmortem

OPEN-WEIGHTS ROUNDUP
A 14B multilingual model from a Tokyo group, a 3B on-device model with surprisingly good tool-calling, and a Ferrite-70B fine-tune for legal clauses. Links: https://latentdispatch.ai/p/ow-roundup-0921

SHORT TAKES
· Quillon-M adds an "unreadable" flag per field instead of guessing. The right design.
· Marrow Speech drops per-minute price 20%.
· Larkspur publishes a migration guide from the two frameworks it is replacing.

